      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records for the closest structural analogs, ribavirin (M04) and levovirin (M03), show substantial plasma Cmax/AUC after oral dosing (e.g., ribavirin Cmax 630 ng/mL and AUC0-12 3326 ng·h/mL; levovirin Cmax 7.8–35 µg/mL across doses), consistent with meaningful oral absorption; none of these records provides a matched oral/IV F below 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C58", "C80", "C77", "C84", "C62", "C74", "C100", "C63", "C59"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The query's computed polarity and ionization (logD -4.16, neutral fraction 0.04, TPSA 151 Å²) are physicochemical caveats, but no affirmative threshold-relevant experimental evidence supports F < 20%; didanosine variability (C35, C42) is a transferability caveat, not a query-specific low outcome.",
      "card_ids": ["C35", "C42"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "oral_auc_cmax_exposure",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C58", "C80", "C77", "C84", "C62", "C74", "C100", "C63", "C59"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability, human PK, permeability, metabolism, or transporter data for the query molecule.",
    "L3 exposure records for ribavirin/levovirin lack IV comparators and dose-normalized F values, so they cannot independently establish the 20% threshold.",
    "Levovirin exposure was measured after oral prodrug R1518, so it may overstate absorption of the parent nucleoside.",
    "The query is more polar and more ionized at pH 7.4 (neutral fraction 0.04, logD -4.16) than the reference nucleosides, so transfer is indirect.",
    "No formulation, dose, or prandial-state information is available for the query.",
    "Didanosine variability (C35, C42) illustrates that polar nucleosides can have F near or below 20% in some populations, but no transferable direct low outcome for the query is available."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) because all transferable measured oral-bioavailability contexts for polar nucleosides/glycosides are >=20% (emtricitabine 92%, stavudine 61–78%, zidovudine 61%, didanosine 22–42%, salicin 43%), and L3 oral exposure for the closest analogs ribavirin/levovirin shows substantial absorption with no direct low-F evidence. The physicochemical low prior is insufficient alone; confidence remains moderate because the query is more polar/ionized and no direct query PK data exist."
}

